// "The bound revenant fights at the caster's command until the binding
// fails" -- same real-agent `SummonInfo::Npc` shape as animate_dead.ron in
// this folder (see that file's header for the full precedent trail), not
// the decorative-phantasm recipe. The difference from animate_dead.ron:
// this is a `Concentration(60)` spell in the sheet, a bound spirit that
// only holds while concentration lasts rather than a permanent thrall, so
// `duration: Some(60s)` is set (matching unseen_servant.ron's own use of a
// finite `duration` on this same recipe, just on the real-agent side of the
// fork instead of the phantasm side).
//
// `body`: `BipedSmall(Jiangshi)` -- a different already-shipped Necromancy
// dungeon undead (assets/common/entity/dungeon/terracotta/jiangshi.ron,
// `CreatureKind::Undead`) than animate_dead.ron's Husk, matching the sheet's
// own "restless spirit... corporeal form" (a possessed/animated revenant)
// framing as distinct from animate_dead's raised corpse. `Strigoi`
// (biped_large) was considered and rejected: that body is the Vampire
// dungeon's miniboss-tier enemy (loot table `dungeon.vampire.miniboss`),
// far outside this level-3 player spell's power band.
//
// `loadout_config`/`skillset_config`: `Preset::JiangshiSummon` already
// exists for this exact body (loadout_builder.rs) -- reused here instead of
// leaving the revenant unarmed, matching the fix applied to
// animate_dead.ron's Husk sibling.
BasicSummon(
    buildup_duration: 1.0,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    summon_info: Npc(
        summoned_amount: 1,
        summon_distance: (1.0, 2.0),
        body: BipedSmall((species: Jiangshi, body_type: Male)),
        scale: None,
        has_health: true,
        use_npc_name: true,
        loadout_config: Some(JiangshiSummon),
        skillset_config: Some(Rank5),
        duration: Some((secs: 60, nanos: 0)),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Arcane), cooldown: Some(45.0)),
)
